// VEI (Volatility Environment Index)
//
// See @link https://www.reddit.com/r/algotrading/comments/1phv4zz/the_signal_i_use_to_detect_hidden_instability_in/
//
// VEI = ATR(10) / ATR(50), measuring short-term volatility vs. the market’s baseline.
//
// Regimes:
// - VEI < 1.0 → Stable/normal conditions; trend & pullback setups behave cleanly
// - VEI > 1.2 → Volatility expansion; noisy trends, fakeouts, more stop-outs
// - VEI < 1.0 → Controlled contraction; highly structured, trend/pullback-friendly
//
// Use VEI as:
// - A market stability / regime filter and risk-management tool
// - To decide when your strategy’s conditions are favorable (position sizing, skipping trades)
//
// VEI is NOT:
// - A buy/sell signal, directional tool, or predictor — it gatekeeps *whether* you should trade, not *where* to enter.


//@version=5

indicator("VEI - Volatility Expansion Index)", overlay=false)

// Settings
shortATR = input.int(10, "ATR Short Length")
longATR = input.int(50, "ATR Long Length")
threshold = input.float(1.2, "Expansion Threshold")

// ATR calculations
atr_short = ta.atr(shortATR)
atr_long = ta.atr(longATR)

// VEI calculation
vei = atr_short / atr_long

// Plot VEI
plot(vei, color=color.new(color.gray, 0), linewidth=1, title="VEI")
// Plot threshold line
hline(threshold, "VEI Threshold", color=color.orange, linewidth=1)
// Simple color change
bgcolor(vei > threshold ? color.new(color.red, 85) : na)

